# Everything the build produces lives in build/ and none of it belongs in the repository. The
# suffixed ones are cross builds — `make BUILD=build-mips CC=mipsel-openwrt-linux-gcc` and its
# aarch64 twin — kept apart so that measuring one target does not throw away the other.
build/
build-*/

# Downloaded once and reused: cross toolchains, mostly. Deliberately NOT under build/, because
# `make clean` empties that — and emptying it once cost a two-hundred-megabyte toolchain and every
# generated fingerprint table on a slow connection. Things that are fetched and things that are
# built have different lifetimes and belong in different places.
dl/

# The Go tooling is built on demand; the binary is not an artefact anyone should be pulling.
tools/fp/fp
tools/fp/fp.exe

# Reports of the automated reference-citation audit, written into the tree by a tool that lives
# outside it. Hundreds of kilobytes of machine output that go stale on the next run: what is worth
# keeping from them ends up in code comments and in DIVERGENCES.md, not here. A report is appended
# to until the run ends, so one without its acceptance section at the bottom may simply be unfinished.
VENDOR.md
VENDOR-REVERSE.md
COVERAGE.md

# The x/text Go ships, copied out of GOROOT for the URL tools by the Makefile.
tools/.goroot-x/

# Python tests and fixture generators leave only local bytecode caches.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
